WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.220
​It takes a mighty hero to tell Captain
Marvel to cool it.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:09.059
Natalie Portman, who will reprise her role
as Jane Foster in the upcoming ​Thor: Love

00:00:09.059 --> 00:00:13.920
and Thunder,​ had a few choice words for
fellow MCU star Brie Larson after the actress

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.560
posted an Instagram shot of herself wielding
Thor's legendary hammer.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:23.500
In case you weren't aware, Portman won't simply
be returning as the Odinson's love interest

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.349
in Love and Thunder; she'll be taking up the
mantle of Mighty Thor herself, following her

00:00:28.349 --> 00:00:32.000
character's recent trajectory in the pages
of Marvel comics.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.100
It appears that, at least for awhile, there
will be two Thors and as far as Portman is

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.940
concerned, there's no room for a third.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:45.080
Earlier this week, Captain Marvel and Avengers:
Endgame star Larson posted a photo to her

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.180
Instagram, which appears to have been taken
in an office at Marvel Studios.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.120
Larson captioned the image:

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.040
"Not to be whatever, but…

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.760
I told you I could lift it."

00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:00.040
Larson's caption is a reference to a 2018
interview with Buzzfeed Brasil, during which

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.140
she was asked whether Captain Marvel could
lift Thor's hammer.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.160
She responded with an enthusiastic "definitely."

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.760
It took her a little while to get around to
proving it….

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.420
"I have nothing to prove to you."

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:16.160
...but never say that the good Captain doesn't
put her money where her mouth is.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.720
Larson’s post has so far garnered over 1.8
million likes, but sharp-eyed Instagram users

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.870
noticed that Portman was quick to chime in
with a response.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:25.870
Portman wrote:

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.800
"Hey muscles, easy with my hammer!!!"

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.800
Portman's remark has amassed over 50,000 likes
of its own, and the display of good-natured

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:39.240
rivalry between two of the MCU's biggest female
stars prompted an outpouring of love from

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.160
fans.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:44.780
Black Panther star Michael B. Jordan also
chipped in with a couple of laughing emojis.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:49.060
The announcement of Portman's return to the
Marvel fold was one of the biggest surprises

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:54.030
of the studio's San Diego Comic-Con 2019 panel,
and it seems like Foster's already getting

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.260
excited to wield Thor's hammer.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:01.820
It's always great to see these displays of
camaraderie between Marvel's stars, but unfortunately,

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:05.740
it seems like it'll be awhile before we see
either of them on the big screen again.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:12.139
Thor: Love and Thunder won't hit the big screen
until November 5, 2021, and a likely sequel

00:02:12.139 --> 00:02:16.020
to Captain Marvel wasn't discussed during
Marvel's Comic-Con panel.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:20.360
Hopefully, when Mighty Thor meets Captain
Marvel for the first time, she'll like the

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.220
cosmic hero as much as her predecessor did.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:29.640
"I like this one."

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:35.360
Marvel's Phase 4 will be significantly shorter
than previous phases, running only through

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:40.769
2021 and consisting of five feature films:
Black Widow, The Eternals, Shang-Chi and the

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:45.800
Legend of the Ten Rings, Doctor Strange in
the Multiverse of Madness, and Thor: Love

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:46.720
and Thunder.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:52.319
So far, only one Phase 5 film has been officially
announced: Blade, which will star Mahershala

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.880
Ali in the title role.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:58.160
Assuming that Phase 5 will also span a couple
of years, it's highly likely that we'll see

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:04.260
Larson's Carol Danvers back on the big screen
sometime in 2022, or 2023 at the latest.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:09.980
It's also not clear how large or small a role
Portman's Mighty Thor will play in the MCU

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:15.319
going forward; perhaps, once series star Chris
Hemsworth hangs up the hammer for good, Portman's

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.940
Foster will carry the franchise a little further.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:22.720
It could also be that some Phase 5 guest appearances
are in the cards, possibly even in Avengers

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:23.780
5.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:29.460
Fans are already hoping that the as-yet unannounced
movie will be a massive crossover which could

00:03:29.469 --> 00:03:34.949
feature the likes of the X-Men and Fantastic
Four, newly available to the MCU after parent

00:03:34.949 --> 00:03:37.879
company Disney's acquisition of 20th Century
Fox.

00:03:37.879 --> 00:03:42.350
We'll just have to wait to see what the future
holds for these two mighty heroes, but in

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:46.520
the meantime, we'll just have to make do with
some winking Instagram banter.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.940
There's probably more where this came from.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:52.939
It turns out that, just like the rest of us,
it's tough for even superheroes to resist

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:55.560
taking friendly pot-shots at each other on
social media.

